    "languageName": "Kiswahili",
    "indigenous": "Hishima ya kiungwana, hujua atendewayo.",
    "literalTranslation": "(It is) the honour of the gentle sort—he recognizes benefits (lit. knows the things which are done for him).",
    "meaning": "(It is) the honour of the gentle sort—he recognizes benefits (lit. knows the things which are done for him).",
    "theme": "unity",
    "sourceCitation": "Rev. W. E. Taylor, M.A. (1891) 'African Aphorisms; or, Saws from Swahili-Land' (SPCK, London), Swahili Proverb #96"
