    "languageName": "Kiswahili",
    "indigenous": "Howe! nda mwenyi kufuma: wewe una Howe! gani?",
    "literalTranslation": "\"There then!\" is for the man that hits: what have you to do with \"There then?\" (Lit. What Howé! have you?).",
    "meaning": "A rebuke to the man who plumes himself on some achievement.",
    "theme": "wisdom",
    "sourceCitation": "Rev. W. E. Taylor, M.A. (1891) 'African Aphorisms; or, Saws from Swahili-Land' (SPCK, London), Swahili Proverb #99"
