    "literalTranslation": "Better is godliness than the white turban. (Or, The fear of God is not a white turban.)",
    "meaning": "The white turban is a mark of a devotee, and is affected by all the sect of the Ibâdhia, to which belong the royal family of Zanzibar, and most of the governors of the coast towns. The cowl does not make the monk.",
