    "languageName": "Kiswahili",
    "indigenous": "Kutinda mbuzi kwa ajili ya kinofu.",
    "literalTranslation": "To slaughter a goat for the sake of a chop.",
    "meaning": "To slaughter a goat for the sake of a chop.",
    "theme": "wisdom",
    "sourceCitation": "Rev. W. E. Taylor, M.A. (1891) 'African Aphorisms; or, Saws from Swahili-Land' (SPCK, London), Swahili Proverb #199"
