    "meaning": "Bitter truth is better than sweet falsehood.",
    "theme": "wisdom",
    "sourceCitation": "Rev. W. E. Taylor, M.A. (1891) 'African Aphorisms; or, Saws from Swahili-Land' (SPCK, London), Swahili Proverb #209"
