    "indigenous": "Wafile maji, na p'ondo kiima-ima.",
    "literalTranslation": "They have died of drowning—and the pole was touching the bottom!",
    "meaning": "See § 387 and note. It means either that they might easily have avoided such a fate: or that it was so that people might see that Divine vengeance had a hand in their death by such an inadequate cause. But it may be applied to any troubles from which, under ordinary circumstances, there would have been an easy escape.",
    "theme": "wisdom",
